<section class="care-guide-page" style="padding: 48px 0 80px; background: var(--color-bg);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 860px;">
    {% render 'breadcrumbs' %}

    <div style="text-align: center; max-width: 600px; margin: 16px auto 48px;">
      <span class="badge badge-editorial" style="margin-bottom: 10px;">LONGEVITY & PRESERVATION</span>
      <h1 class="heading-serif" style="font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3rem);">
        Yarn & Care Guide
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size: 15px; color: rgba(51,44,40,0.8); line-height: 1.6; margin-top: 8px;">
        Handmade crochet pieces are heirloom treasures made from natural fibers. Follow these simple steps to keep them pristine for years.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 3 Big Care Cards -->
    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 24px;">
      
      <div style="background: #FFF; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); border: 1px solid var(--color-beige); padding: 32px; box-shadow: var(--shadow-subtle);">
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
          <div style="width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--color-bg); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; color: var(--color-brown); font-weight: 700;">1</div>
          <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-text);">Washing Your Pieces</h2>
        </div>
        <ul style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(51,44,40,0.85); line-height: 1.7; padding-left: 20px; list-style-type: disc;">
          <li>Always <strong>hand wash in cool or lukewarm water</strong> (below 30°C / 86°F).</li>
          <li>Use a gentle, pH-neutral liquid detergent formulated for delicate cotton or wool.</li>
          <li>Submerge and gently press the water through the stitches. <em>Never vigorously scrub, rub, or stretch the knit.</em></li>
          <li>Avoid bleach, harsh enzymes, or fabric softeners as they degrade natural fiber strength.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="background: #FFF; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); border: 1px solid var(--color-beige); padding: 32px; box-shadow: var(--shadow-subtle);">
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
          <div style="width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--color-bg); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; color: var(--color-brown); font-weight: 700;">2</div>
          <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-text);">Drying & Reshaping</h2>
        </div>
        <ul style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(51,44,40,0.85); line-height: 1.7; padding-left: 20px; list-style-type: disc;">
          <li><strong>Never wring or twist</strong> the crochet piece; doing so distorts the stitch gauge.</li>
          <li>Lay the garment flat on a clean dry towel, roll it up into a cylinder, and press gently to absorb excess water.</li>
          <li>Unroll, gently reshape to its original dimensions, and <strong>lay flat to dry in the shade</strong> on a drying rack.</li>
          <li><strong>Never machine tumble dry</strong> or hang wet crochet on hangers (gravity will stretch it out).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="background: #FFF; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); border: 1px solid var(--color-beige); padding: 32px; box-shadow: var(--shadow-subtle);">
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
          <div style="width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--color-bg); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; color: var(--color-brown); font-weight: 700;">3</div>
          <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-text);">Storage & Maintenance</h2>
        </div>
        <ul style="font-size: 14px; color: rgba(51,44,40,0.85); line-height: 1.7; padding-left: 20px; list-style-type: disc;">
          <li>Store garments <strong>folded flat</strong> inside breathable cotton dust bags or drawers.</li>
          <li>Avoid hanging tops and cardigans on wire hangers to prevent shoulder distortion.</li>
          <li>If a thread snag occurs, <em>never cut it</em>! Use a crochet hook or bobby pin to pull the loop back to the interior side.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Care Guide Page",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
